flowchart TB
  accTitle: Unneeded data can remain reachable
  accDescr: A global retaining root keeps the object graph reachable. Removing its last retaining path makes that graph eligible for collection. Collection and release of resident pages to the OS are later distinct events.
G["Global retaining root"] -->|strong reference| O["Reachable object graph"]
  O -->|remove last retaining path| U["Unreachable graph
eligible for collection"]
  U -->|collector may reclaim| F["Reusable managed-heap space
RSS release not guaranteed"]
  class O pending;
  class U neutral;
  class F success;

